--- note
CEIL/FLOOR of a number at the integer-digit cap can carry into a 1,000,001st digit; that is E_RANGE at the call, as ROUND already is (spec 6.4). Position 1:1 is the call, the innermost failing node. Observed when written: JS, PHP, Python and Lisp raise E_RANGE but report 0:0 (no position); C++ and Go raise nothing and return a 1,000,001-digit value (GO-C12). Control: CEIL of a negative never carries.
--- source
LEN(CEIL("-" & REPEAT("9", 1000000) & ".5")) - 1
--- expect
